 evaluable at specified timepoint.\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"paramType\":\"MEAN\",\"dispersionType\":\"Standard Deviation\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"percentage of the total cell population\",\"timeFrame\":\"Baseline, Weeks 49 and 73\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Danicopan\",\"description\":\"Participants in this study continued to receive danicopan tablets orally at the same dose (150, 175, or 200 milligrams \\\\[mg\\\\] 3 times daily \\\\[TID\\\\]) that they were receiving upon completion of the primary Study ACH471-100. Dose escalation was done in increments of 25 mg to a maximum of 250 mg TID, in case additional clinical benefit was expected as per Investigator and Sponsor decision.\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"6\"}]}],\"classes\":[{\"title\":\"Change at Week 49\",\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"6\"}]}],\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"30.83\",\"spread\":\"11.531\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Change at Week 73\",\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"5\"}]}],\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"32.00\",\"spread\":\"19.170\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"SECONDARY\",\"title\":\"Change From Baseline in AP Complement Functional Activity at Weeks 49 and 145\",\"description\":\"Serum AP functional activity was measured by the Wieslab functional immunoassay method. Change from Baseline = Serum AP functional activity at specified postbaseline visit - Baseline Serum AP functional activity. Baseline was the baseline value from the primary Study ACH471-100.\",\"populationDescription\":\"Full analysis set included all enrolled and treated participants. Here, 'Overall number of participants analyzed' = participants with both baseline and the postbaseline assessments for Serum AP functional activity. 'Number analyzed' = participants evaluable at specified timepoint.\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"paramType\":\"MEAN\",\"dispersionType\":\"Standard Deviation\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"percentage of activity\",\"timeFrame\":\"Baseline, Weeks 49 and 145\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Danicopan\",\"description\":\"Participants in this study continued to receive danicopan tablets orally at the same dose (150, 175, or 200 milligrams \\\\[mg\\\\] 3 times daily \\\\[TID\\\\]) that they were receiving upon completion of the primary Study ACH471-100. Dose escalation was done in increments of 25 mg to a maximum of 250 mg TID, in case additional clinical benefit was expected as per Investigator and Sponsor decision.\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"6\"}]}],\"classes\":[{\"title\":\"Change at Week 49\",\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"6\"}]}],\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"-59.80\",\"spread\":\"14.217\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Change at Week 145\",\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"2\"}]}],\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"-52.43\",\"spread\":\"2.779\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"SECONDARY\",\"title\":\"Change From Baseline in Free Hgb at Weeks 49 and 169\",\"description\":\"Change from Baseline = free Hgb at specified postbaseline visit - Baseline free Hgb. Baseline was the baseline value from the primary Study ACH471-100.\",\"populationDescription\":\"Full analysis set included all enrolled and treated participants. Here, 'Overall number of participants analyzed' = participants with both baseline and the postbaseline assessments for free Hgb. 'Number analyzed' = participants evaluable at specified timepoint.\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"paramType\":\"MEAN\",\"dispersionType\":\"Standard Deviation\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"mg/dL\",\"timeFrame\":\"Baseline, Weeks 49 and 169\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Danicopan\",\"description\":\"Participants in this study continued to receive danicopan tablets orally at the same dose (150, 175, or 200 milligrams \\\\[mg\\\\] 3 times daily \\\\[TID\\\\]) that they were receiving upon completion of the primary Study ACH471-100. Dose escalation was done in increments of 25 mg to a maximum of 250 mg TID, in case additional clinical benefit was expected as per Investigator and Sponsor decision.\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"6\"}]}],\"classes\":[{\"title\":\"Change at Week 49\",\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"6\"}]}],\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"105.92\",\"spread\":\"92.308\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Change at Week 169\",\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"2\"}]}],\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"-30.75\",\"spread\":\"54.942\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"SECONDARY\",\"title\":\"Change From Baseline in Functional Assessment of Chronic Illness Therapy (FACIT)-Fatigue Scale Score at Weeks 21, 41, and 153\",\"description\":\"The FACIT-Fatigue scale is a collection of quality of life questionnaires pertaining to the management of fatigue symptoms due to a chronic illness. The FACIT-Fatigue is a 13-item questionnaire that assesses self-reported fatigue and its impact upon daily activities and function over the preceding 7 days. Participants score each item on a 5-point scale: 0 (Not at all) to 4 (Very much). Total scores range from 0 to 52, with higher score indicating better quality of life.\",\"populationDescription\":\"Full analysis set included all enrolled and treated participants. Here, 'Overall number of participants analyzed' = participants with both baseline and the postbaseline assessments for FACIT-Fatigue scale score. 'Number analyzed' = participants evaluable at specified timepoint.\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"paramType\":\"MEAN\",\"dispersionType\":\"Standard Deviation\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"units on a scale\",\"timeFrame\":\"Baseline, Weeks 21, 41, and 153\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Danicopan\",\"description\":\"Participants in this study continued to receive danicopan tablets orally at the same dose (150, 175, or 200 milligrams \\\\[mg\\\\] 3 times daily \\\\[TID\\\\]) that they were receiving upon completion of the primary Study ACH471-100. Dose escalation was done in increments of 25 mg to a maximum of 250 mg TID, in case additional clinical benefit was expected as per Investigator and Sponsor decision.\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"8\"}]}],\"classes\":[{\"title\":\"Change at Week 21\",\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"8\"}]}],\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"8.4\",\"spread\":\"11.75\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Change at Week 41\",\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"7\"}]}],\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"9.1\",\"spread\":\"13.37\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Change at Week 153\",\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"2\"}]}],\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"3.0\",\"spread\":\"0.00\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"SECONDARY\",\"title\":\"Change From Baseline in European Organisation for Research and Treatment of Cancer, Quality of Life Questionnaire-Core 30 Scale (EORTC-QLQ-C30): Global Health Status/Qol Score at Weeks 21, 41, and 153\",\"description\":\"EORTC-QLQ-C30 is comprised of 30 questions. First 28 questions used 4-point scale (1=not at all,2=a little,3=quite a bit,4=very much) for evaluating 5 functional scales (physical, role, emotional, cognitive, social), 3 symptom scales (fatigue, nausea/vomiting, pain) \\\\& other single items. For each item, high score = high level of symptomatology/problem. Last 2 questions represented participant's assessment of overall health (global health status) and quality of life, coded on 7-point scale (1=very poor to 7=excellent). Answers were converted into grading scale, with total score between 0 and 100. A high score represented a favourable outcome with a best quality of life for participant.\",\"populationDescription\":\"Full analysis set included all enrolled and treated participants. Here, 'Overall number of participants analyzed' = participants with both baseline and the postbaseline assessments for EORTC-QLQ-C30 (Global Health Status/Qol) score. 'Number analyzed' = participants evaluable at specified timepoint.\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"paramType\":\"MEAN\",\"dispersionType\":\"Standard Deviation\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"units on a scale\",\"timeFrame\":\"Baseline, Weeks 21, 41, and 153\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Danicopan\",\"description\":\"Participants in this study continued to receive danicopan tablets orally at the same dose (150, 175, or 200 milligrams \\\\[mg\\\\] 3 times daily \\\\[TID\\\\]) that they were receiving upon completion of the primary Study ACH471-100. Dose escalation was done in increments of 25 mg to a maximum of 250 mg TID, in case additional clinical benefit was expected as per Investigator and Sponsor decision.\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"8\"}]}],\"classes\":[{\"title\":\"Change at Week 21\",\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"8\"}]}],\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"16.67\",\"spread\":\"25.973\"}]}]},{\"title\":\"Change at Week 41\",\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"7\"}]}],\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"11.90\",\"spread\":\"29.603\"}]}]},{